// Linux x86-64 socket binding, emitted in Sayanox like sxlimit/CI guards.
// This fixed kernel-only bridge owns socket/bind/listen/accept/connect/read/
// write/close, bounded 8192-byte private-pipe frames, and parent-death cleanup.
// HTTP routing, parsing, responses, fixture state and assertions are Sayanox.
// Leaf protocol: port/PID handshake (server), A, W<8 hex bytes>\n<payload>
// -> OK; R\n -> <8 hex count>\n<payload>; C\n closes the connection.
// Syscall reads/writes retry EINTR and finish partial private-pipe transfers.
